id: pm-agent-token-path
title: Agent-task token ratchet changes verdict with temporary-root path length
description: "The unchanged agent-task replay exceeds published Plan mutation and composite token ceilings when TMPDIR has a longer external path, because advertised recovery commands contain that physical path. A canonical short-root replay passes unchanged. This is a fixture portability gap; do not raise token budgets or claim a product-output regression without separating incidental root length from meaningful output."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-08T05:13:12.301Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-09T12:10:30.942Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-09T11:59:31.196Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-09T11:59:31.196Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: The same tree yields the same token-gate verdict beneath short and long safe temporary roots; independently reported emitted bytes remain truthful; recovery commands remain executable against the actual fixture; negative controls still reject real output growth.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "Version 5 compares narrowly canonicalized Plan recovery suffixes only after exact transport accounting and payload parity pass. Reports retain raw bytes/tokens and actual executable commands. Task, step, orientation and composite comparisons use explicit versioned normalized measurements and refuse invalid values or scope drift. Composite ceiling tightens 13882 to 13795 with no increases."
expected_result: "Physical temporary path lengths do not change the verdict, while growing semantic output, false accounting or invalid recovery still fail."
actual_result: "Real short/long temporary-root replays both compared at 13795 tokens while raw costs remained 13887 versus 14027. Existing million-token growth control detected regression; meaningful retained path facts still increase cost. Linked gate tests, full source coverage at 100/100/100/100, strict agent-token, source assurance, context, mutation and packed consumer gates pass."
