comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-08T05:13:12.301Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status 2905-item corpus and the newly created ancestor item, targeted title/description plus metadata search, refreshed open/in-progress lists, and full live pm-8pnj/pm-aksavu/pm-4o7tlx/pm-95h7pg reads. Historical fixes covered accounting validity or ambient warning/env leakage, not recovery-path length. Current evidence: longer-root Plan task 894 vs 848 tokens, add 298 vs 275, complete 297 vs 274, composite 13883 vs 13882; unchanged short-root replay exits 0. Remains open and unclaimed while the four selected fixes finish."
  "2026-10-09T11:00:44.149Z","harness:codex","TDD regression: after correcting the fixture shell quoting, the retained Plan parity test fails specifically because comparison_estimated_tokens is absent. The test compares short and long external roots, requires different actual emitted bytes, and preserves estimated_tokens=ceil(actual emitted_bytes/4). Scope is only independently validated Plan recovery suffixes, not arbitrary payload paths or contents."
  "2026-10-09T11:06:20.862Z","harness:codex","Post-fix focused suite passed the Plan path, accounting, parity and measurement controls. Generated v5 baseline comparison scope is explicit, composite ceiling tightened from 13882 to 13795 estimated tokens and no task or step ceiling increased. Plan mutation task tightened 848 to 806. Original emitted bytes/tokens remain separately retained."
  "2026-10-09T11:30:32.229Z","harness:codex","Real independent transcript replay under a short temporary root and a long root with spaces produced identical normalized composite comparison=13795, while exact raw composite costs remained 13887 versus 14027. The existing million-token negative control returned the expected detected regression. The negative-control wrapper returns success when detection succeeds; an initial orchestration check assumed a nonzero wrapper exit and was corrected without changing the production predicate or baseline."
  "2026-10-09T11:31:21.627Z","harness:codex","Cross-project intake: strict all-status corpus and live metadata/history preserve historical completed work. All 18 open GitHub issues have PM-link comments; initial open PR, Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning counts were zero. Full graph audit retained 14911 deduplicated edges, 14844 informative, no ordering contradiction or isolated active item; historical hierarchy advisories and 170 missing-resolution warnings remain visible. Fresh required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with no critical/high Sentry findings, and one-day telemetry reports 4830 finishes, 0.87% failures and zero missing error-code rows. These are current observations, separate from hosted release success and permanent queue drainage."
  "2026-10-09T11:40:54.710Z","harness:codex","Full final-source coverage passed 9958 tests with zero uncovered source counts: lines 64101/64101, statements 67275/67275, functions 13870/13870, branches 51487/51487. All owner-linked tests passed through pm test with isolated schema context. Final candidate/control npm and Bun manual sessions each passed 13 steps with real population, complete SDK read, observed refusal/recovery status and original output ceilings. The earlier full run failed a host npm-module resolution prerequisite and remains a failed receipt; enabling the installed global npm module resolved it without changing source or tests. Final static/context/packed consumer chain is running and closure awaits its result."
  "2026-10-09T12:10:30.942Z","harness:codex","Final pre-PR aggregate validation passed: fresh complete pnpm quality:static, typecheck, source exact coverage, context/token surface, doc/skill links, tracked-file secret scan, dependency audit, all linked checks, npm/npx/Bun/bunx packed consumers and 89-command package-first dogfood. Latest npm pm-changelog 2026.10.5 generated the four actual closures under Unreleased; its check passed. Final distribution 19952672 bytes is below the unchanged 20000000-byte base budget. Historical 170 missing-resolution warnings and known prose gaps remain explicit. All four implemented owners are closed/released; the separately reproduced schema-field transport owner stays open/unclaimed. Hosted review and exact-tag publication recovery remain separate upcoming verifications."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
